findings:
FEAT-002 contract (all in place and verified via lint + build):

EXPORTED TYPES (from `@/types`, src/types/index.ts):
- IHazardAlert { signalLevel: 1|2|3|4|5; typhoonName: string; affectedAreas: string[]; timestamp: string; severity: "advisory"|"warning"|"emergency" }
- IEvacuationCenter { name: string; distance: string; capacity: string; directionsUrl: string }
- IHotline { label: string; number: string; tel: string }
- IAlertState { hasActiveHazard: boolean; alert: IHazardAlert | null; evacuationCenters: IEvacuationCenter[]; hotlines: IHotline[]; source: string; fetchedAt: string }

API ROUTE: GET /api/alerts (src/app/api/alerts/route.ts) returns Response.json(IAlertState). `export const revalidate = 900` (confirmed 15m in build route table). Success payload: source "mock", hasActiveHazard true, sample typhoon (signalLevel 3, typhoonName "Bagyong Pepito", affectedAreas incl. "Calamba, Laguna"/"CALABARZON", severity "warning"), 2 evacuation centers, 3 hotlines. On error: 200 fallback with hasActiveHazard false, alert null, empty centers, same hotlines, source "fallback" (never 500/throws). Hotlines are 911 (tel:911), Philippine Red Cross 143 (tel:143), NDRRMC "(02) 8911-1406 / 911-5061" (tel:+6328911406).

HOOK: useAlerts() exported from `@/hooks` barrel (src/hooks/index.ts). Return shape: { state: IAlertState | null; loading: boolean; error: string | null; refetch: () => void }. Fetches /api/alerts on mount and on refetch(); writes success to localStorage; on failure restores cache and sets a Filipino error string. error is null on success; Filipino strings on failure (connection message, with a "(maaaring luma na)" variant when cache is stale > 900000ms, and a no-cache variant).

localStorage KEY: "klimaguard:lastAlertState" storing JSON { state: IAlertState; cachedAt: number } (cachedAt = Date.now() ms). Staleness threshold 900000ms (15 min).

ENV NOTE: worktree had NO node_modules initially; ran `npm ci` in the worktree to populate it (shares the committed package-lock). Build (Turbopack) rejects a node_modules symlink/junction pointing outside the project root, so a local install is required for build verification. node_modules is gitignored and not committed.

NOT DONE (FEAT-002 scope): AlertBanner.tsx, EvacuationCard.tsx, components/alerts/index.ts barrel, app/alerts/page.tsx, and mounting <AlertBanner/> in layout.tsx. README update hook fired but was intentionally left to FEAT-002/UI work to avoid conflicting with the concurrent M2+M8 branch and to keep FEAT-001 edits scoped.
